package:
  name: hdllint.z0i
  desc: 0-in lint integration (`0in`)
  doc: |
    0-in as a lint tool. It runs `0in -lint <files> -top <top>` and
    parses the 0-in text report into normalized findings.

    It implements the `Rtl` family and no other.

    0-in is the property of its respective owners.

  imports:
  - name: hdllint

  tasks:
  - export: Rtl
    uses: hdllint.Rtl
    desc: Runs 0-in lint and reports normalized findings
    doc: |
      The `hdllint.Rtl` family task with `tools:` pinned to 0-in.
      Identical in every other respect -- same waivers, same baseline, same
      reports.

      Use this when a flow wants 0-in specifically; use `hdllint.Rtl`
      when it wants whatever lint tools are available.

      ```yaml
      - name: lint
        uses: hdllint.z0i.Rtl
        needs: [rtl]
        with:
          top: [my_top]
          profile: strict
      ```

      Profiles map to 0-in flags as:

      | profile   | flags            |
      |-----------|------------------|
      | `basic`   | (defaults)       |
      | `default` | `-full`          |
      | `strict`  | `-full -all`     |
    with:
      tools:
        type: list
        value: [z0i]
